{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>and I will greatly multiply your seed</b> Three times in the Masorah: זרעך in this parashah — corresponding to three times \"seed\" by which Israel is called: זרע ברך ה' בני זרע אברהם — corresponding to Abraham, as written: וה' ברך את אברהם בכל. זרע קדש מצבתה — corresponding to Isaac, who sanctified the name of the Holy One, blessed be He. כלה זרע אמת — corresponding to Jacob, whose bed was complete (שלימה), and that is what is written: תתן אמת ליעקב." "<b>like the sand</b> Two times in the Masorah: this one, and the other: וכחול ארבה ימים. And this is what is said: כי כימי העץ ימי עמי — for He likewise promised them length of days."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The three Hebrew phrases (זרע ברך ה' בני זרע אברהם; זרע קדש מצבתה; כלה זרע אמת) are masoretic catchphrases identifying three occurrences of the word זרע applied to Israel. I preserved them in Hebrew script as masorah quotations; the wordplay linking each to a patriarch stays implicit as in the original.", 1 "The verse cited כי כימי העץ ימי עמי is Isaiah 65:22; the second masoretic occurrence וכחול ארבה ימים is Genesis 32:13. Addresses not written by the author are not added inline."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:43.576416826Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}